 "notes": [
  "Fix: wire3 previously shared hole 6b.f with the pushbutton leg 2.l. It now goes into 6b.g, the same 5-hole strip (column 6, bottom half), so it is still electrically joined to button side 2.",
  "Parts are unchanged from step 1; no parts added or dropped.",
  "Circuit: 5V and GND go to the top rails; the top rails are bridged to the bottom rails by wire8 (black, -) and wire9 (red, +). Each FSR is a voltage divider: one leg to the + rail, the other to a column strip shared with a 10K resistor to the - rail and a yellow wire to A0 (sensor 1) or A1 (sensor 2).",
  "Pushbutton: the catalogue says legs 1.l/1.r are one side and 2.l/2.r the other, with the centre gap between sides. Side 1 (top half) carries pin 2 (blue wire, 7t.b) and the 10K pull-down r3 (6t.c to 10t.c, with wire4 taking 10t.d to the - rail). Side 2 (bottom half) carries 5V from the + rail via wire3 (tp.5 to 6b.g). This matches the schematic.",
  "Hole labels follow the catalogue convention (t = rows a-e, b = rows f-j) and are placed for electrical correctness; exact columns differ slightly from the picture, where the sensors share columns with the button.",
  "The FSR leads in the picture (red and blue) are treated as part of the FSR; its two terminals go to the + rail and to the divider column."
